r students Hispanohablantes International students Military, veterans Graduate, online + adult learners Students w/ intellectual disabilities Parents + families Tuition + financial aid Tuition + financial aid Housing + food rates Scholarships Fees + other cost info Online bill payment Student consumer info Apply + enroll How to apply Admission requirements Enrollment deposit RED101 Days Raider Nation Orientation Campus life Focused and fun Your Northwestern education doesn’t stop when class is over. Some of the best lessons for life happen in your residence hall, on the court, during rehearsal, on a mission trip … Campus life @ NWC Community life Performing arts Campus dining Clubs + organizations Sports + fitness Community + belonging Orange City Residence life Residence halls Resident directors What to bring Support + resources Bridge Center Compass Center for Career & Calling Counseling + health Safety + security Student life staff Athletics Work hard. Play hard. At Northwestern, sports is training for life. The Raiders win, but the bigger victory is the lessons in character and commitment that last long after the season is over. Visit nwcraiders.com Men's sports Baseball Basketball Cheerleading Cross country Esports Football Golf Soccer Track + field Wrestling Women's sports Basketball Cheerleading Cross country Dance Esports Golf Soccer Softball Tennis Track + field Volleyball Wrestling Red Raiders Athletic band Camps Facilities Hall of Fame Photo gallery Raider Athletics Association Recruit info Athletics staff Webcast Fitness Center DeWitt Fitness Center Golf Practice Room Hours Fitness staff Faith Faith and courage A Northwestern education is for your head and your heart. Because the world needs people who are more than just smart. It needs brave Christians committed to making a difference. Faith @ NWC Campus ministry Staff Christian formation Calendar Watch + listen live Alumni Spread Red Stay connected to Northwestern by reading the Classic alumni magazine, attending alumni events, and encouraging smart Christian students to check out your alma mater. Alumni @ NWC Connect Classic magazine Shop NWC Compass Center for Career & Calling Meet our grads Update your information Events Calendar Raider Nation Celebration (Homecoming) Get involved Give to NWC Refer a student Distinguished alumni National Alumni Board Work at NWC Giving Mission Investment Giving to Northwestern is more than just making a donation. It’s an investment in Christian higher education and students who will make a difference in God’s world. Giving @ NWC Give now Credit card Support a cause Endowed gifts Raider Athletics Association Theatre Patrons Music Patrons Planned giving Beneficiary designations Charitable gift annuities Charitable lead trusts Charitable remainder trusts Endowed gifts Heritage Society Memorial gifts Real estate Wills and living trusts Resources Advancement staff Update your information About Faith and learning Since 1882, Northwestern has been delivering an excellent education within the context of community and a Christian worldview. About NWC Learn about NWC Academic excellence Community + belonging History + heritage Orange City, Iowa Quick facts Student consumer info Work for NWC Why NWC? Mission and values Our mission Christian identity statement Vision for Learning Vision for Diversity People Leadership President Greg Christy News + Events Information. Invitation. There’s always something going on at Northwestern. Stay current with Northwestern news. Come to campus for concerts, plays, art exhibits, Raider sports and more. News + events @ NWC News & media Press releases Videos Events Campus calendar Alumni events Athletic events Continuing education Music concerts Theatre productions Visual art exhibits Marketing & Communications NWC logos and photos MarCom and web staff MYNWC Your campus connection MyNWC is a Web-based system that allows you to access information about your financial aid, housing assignment, billing status, course schedule and academic records. MyNWC MyNWC Login Blackboard Login Biology Faculty Northwestern College seeks to fill a full-time tenure-track assistant professor position in the department of biology beginning in August of 2027. Ideal candidates will be well rounded in biology and have the ability to teach a broad range of biological courses. The successful candidate will teach introductory anatomy and physiology and upper-level courses in microbiology, cell biology, and/or molecular genetics, depending on the expertise of the candidate. There will also be possible opportunities to teach in areas of specialization within an undergraduate curriculum. The teaching load for this position is 24 credit hours per academic year. The successful candidate will also be responsible for scholarship and service, including recruiting and advising biology students. Northwestern enjoys a strong reputation in the sciences based on the career accomplishments of our faculty and graduates, and on the college’s commitment to courageous and confident inquiry, exploration and discovery of God’s truth as it is revealed through the natural world. Our $24.5 million DeWitt Family Science Center is testimony to our investment in the sciences. Required Qualifications: Applicants should have a Ph.D. in biology or a closely related field to be considered for a tenure track position (ABD will also be considered). Candidates should demonstrate evidence for excellent classroom teaching and engagement in scholarship. Preferred Qualifications: Preferred candidates will have demonstrated experience in higher education and research interests conducive to student involvement. Northwestern College seeks candidates with an authentic Christian faith who will embrace and live out our mission & values , including our Reformed, evangelical and ecumenical identity as stated in our Christian Identity Statement, Mission Statement, Vision for Learning and Vision for Diversity. We view these statements as complementary and draw from each in fulfilling our mission. We seek faculty invested in teaching, a program of scholarly activity, and the mission of excellence in the liberal arts, as a vital expression of commitment to Christ’s redemptive work in the world. Apply online below and send a letter of interest in which you (1) describe your teaching experience and (2) scholarly trajectory; and (3) discuss how the following statements would inform and shape your teaching and scholarship: our Statement of Christian Identity , Vision for Learning and Vision for Diversity . Include a current curriculum vitae/resume and send to [email protected] . Review of applications will begin immediately and continue until the position is filled. Apply online To apply for this position, use the button below to start or resume your application. Apply now Explore Application process Application instructions Employment application Contact us FAQs Benefits Faculty Staff Handbooks Faculty Employee Resources Living in Orange City Insurance MRF Home About Work at NWC Current openings APPLY NOW VISIT CAMPUS NEWS & EVENTS CONTACT US PRIVACY POLICY Facebook Twitter Instagram Linked In YouTube More Social Media © 2026 Northwestern College. 101 7th Street SW • Orange City, Iowa 51041 • All rights reserved. LOADING …"
    },
