ng status, course schedule and academic records. MyNWC MyNWC Login Blackboard Login Assistant Softball Coach Northwestern College is seeking applicants for the position of assistant softball coach. Red Raider softball is seeking a candidate who can assist in leading a nationally contending program that won three consecutive GPAC titles from 2023-2025, and hosted back-to-back NAIA regionals in 2024-2025. Join the excellent Red Raider athletic department that claimed 5 GPAC titles this past year and sent 13 teams to the NAIA postseason. Responsibilities will include working with the head coach to administer and promote the softball program in a manner consistent with the mission and goals of Northwestern’s athletic department. The assistant coach will assist with practices, recruit athletes, and develop positive relationships with fellow coaches and athletes alike. This position will also involve responsibilities that may include teaching in the kinesiology curriculum or additional athletic department duties. The mission of Red Raider athletics is to “Honor Christ Through Excellence in Athletics.” The department core values include grit, gratitude, Christlike, competitive greatness, and focus. The Red Raider athletic vision seeks to Bring in student-athletes who desire to excel in all aspects of their life, Build them as individuals and athletes during their collegiate athlete experience, and Send them to championships on the competitive surface and ultimately out into the world as graduates of Northwestern College. A bachelor’s degree is required with master’s preferred, but all qualified candidates for the position will be considered. Applicants must possess excellent knowledge of the sport of softball and have experience as a softball coach at the college or high school level. Northwestern College seeks candidates with an authentic Christian faith who will embrace and live out our mission & values , including our Reformed, evangelical and ecumenical identity as stated in our Christian Identity Statement, Mission Statement, Vision for Learning and Vision for Diversity. We view these statements as complementary and draw from each in fulfilling our mission. Apply online below and send letter of application and resume to [email protected] . Apply online To apply for this position, use the button below to start or resume your application. Apply now Explore Application process Application instructions Employment application Contact us FAQs Benefits Faculty Staff Handbooks Faculty Employee Resources Living in Orange City Insurance MRF Home About Work at NWC Current openings APPLY NOW VISIT CAMPUS NEWS & EVENTS CONTACT US PRIVACY POLICY Facebook Twitter Instagram Linked In YouTube More Social Media © 2026 Northwestern College. 101 7th Street SW • Orange City, Iowa 51041 • All rights reserved. LOADING …"
