urse schedule and academic records. MyNWC MyNWC Login Blackboard Login Housekeeper Northwestern College is seeking a 3/4-time housekeeper for the maintenance department. This position is year-round, requiring 20 hours per week during the academic year, and 40 hours per week in the summer, which may involve working evenings or weekends during special events. The ideal candidate will have prior custodial experience. Supervisory experience is preferred. Candidates must have the ability to perform physically demanding work and be able to regularly lift 10 to 30 pounds and occasionally lift up to 40 pounds. Good communication skills are also essential, as the person in this position regularly greets the public and communicates with parents and students and will supervise several student employees. Northwestern College seeks candidates with an authentic Christian faith who will embrace and live out our mission & values , including our Reformed, evangelical and ecumenical identity as stated in our Christian Identity Statement, Mission Statement, Vision for Learning and Vision for Diversity. We view these statements as complementary and draw from each in fulfilling our mission. Apply online below and send letter of application and resume to [email protected] . Apply online To apply for this position, use the button below to start or resume your application. Apply now Explore Application process Application instructions Employment application Contact us FAQs Benefits Faculty Staff Handbooks Faculty Employee Resources Living in Orange City Insurance MRF Home About Work at NWC Current openings APPLY NOW VISIT CAMPUS NEWS & EVENTS CONTACT US PRIVACY POLICY Facebook Twitter Instagram Linked In YouTube More Social Media © 2026 Northwestern College. 101 7th Street SW • Orange City, Iowa 51041 • All rights reserved. LOADING …"
